— per-agent credentials for self-bond/reporting and wallet-bound lottery entitlements.\n\n## AIMarket\n\nFavorite\n\nAI & Machine LearningPayments & BillingAgent Orchestration\n\nby alexar76\n\nPython\n\nHybrid\n\n### Server Configuration\n\nDescribes the environment variables required to run the server.\n\nName  | Required  | Description  | Default\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n`AIMARKET_PQC`  | No  | Set to `1` to sign hybrid (Ed25519 + ML-DSA-65); back up `<key>_mldsa` together with the Ed25519 key.  | \n`DATABASE_URL`  | No  | PostgreSQL for production — when set, every subsystem shares it; mandatory when `AIFACTORY_PROD=1`. Non-postgres values fail at startup in production.  | \n`AIFACTORY_PROD`  | No  | `1` puts every money gate on the production path (on-chain verification required, fail-closed defaults).  | \n`AIMARKET_DB_PATH`  | No  | The hub index database. It no longer overrides a path a subsystem passes explicitly; a subsystem that must share the hub file now points its own variable at it.  | data/hub.db\n`AIMARKET_HUB_URL`  | No  | Public URL of the hub (used in receipts and well-known documents). Mandates also name it in their audience.  | http://localhost:9083\n`AIMARKET_HUB_NAME`  | No  | Display name in manifests.  | AIMarket Hub\n`AIMARKET_SEED_LIST`  | No  | Comma-separated peer `.well-known` URLs; unset falls back to the shipped seed file, not to \"no seeds\".  | \n`AIMARKET_ADMIN_TOKEN`  | No  | Operator token. Unset ⇒ every admin route refuses (`503`), fail-closed. Same token gates the /operator desk.  | \n`AIMARKET_AGENT_TOKENS`  | No  | `agent-a:secretA,…` — per-agent credentials for self-bond/reporting and wallet-bound lottery entitlements.  | \n`AIMARKET_CORS_ORIGINS`  | No  | Comma-separated allowlist. Empty means no cross-origin access (a `*` default enabled drive-by CSRF).  | \n`AIMARKET_SEED_PUBKEYS`  | No  | `{url:key}` JSON or `url=key,…` — trusted-on-first-contact only; rotating an existing DB pin requires `POST /federation/peers/repin`. 